{
  "dom_id": "step-q270234",
  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Write $\\frac{8{x}^{2}}{4x-5}$ in the form $ax+\\frac{bx}{4x-5},$ where $a\\ne 0.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">$8{x}^{2}$</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\" align=\"center\">$=$</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\" align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\" align=\"center\">$x\\,+\\,$</td>\n<td width=\"50\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">$4x-5$</td>\n<td width=\"25\" height=\"25\" align=\"center\">$4x-5$</td>\n\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
  "worked_solution": "First, we factor the numerator to put $4x$ in parentheses. Then, we subtract and add $5$ in the parentheses. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8{x}^{2}}{4x-5} & =\\frac{2x(4x)}{4x-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x(4x-5+5)}{4x-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x[(4x-5)+(5)]}{4x-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x(4x-5)+2x(5)}{4x-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x(4x-5)+10x}{4x-5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x(4x-5)+10x}{4x-5} & =\\frac{2x(4x-5)}{4x-5}+\\frac{10x}{4x-5} \\\\  & =2x+\\frac{10x}{4x-5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
